      "description": "Watch Flamengo vs Independiente del Valle highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 17, 2026. The CONMEBOL Libertadores delivered another night of intense drama on September 17, 2026 , as Flamengo hosted Independiente del Valle . With both sides desperate for points in this continental showdown, the atmosphere was electric from the opening whistle. Visitors Strike First in the First Half The match began with Independiente del Valle demonstrating their tactical discipline and clinical edge. The breakthrough came in the 31st minute when Djorkaeff Reasco found the back of the net, silencing the home crowd with a well-placed finish. Flamengo struggled to find their rhythm in the opening 45 minutes, often thwarted by a resolute Ecuadorian defense that limited their clear-cut chances before the halftime whistle. Discipline Issues and a Crucial Red Card The intensity ramped up in the second half as tempers flared. Yellow cards were quickly issued to Lucas Paquetá and Jorginho as the pressure mounted. The game took a decisive turn in the 65th minute when Jorginho received his second yellow card, leaving Flamengo to fight with only ten men. Despite the numerical disadvantage, the hosts refused to back down, making several substitutions including the introduction of Giorgian De Arrascaeta to spark a comeback. Late Heroics from De Arrascaeta As the clock ticked toward full time, the ten men of Flamengo produced a moment of magic in the 83rd minute. In a rare occurrence, goalkeeper Agustín Rossi provided the assist for Giorgian De Arrascaeta , who clinicaly finished to level the score at 1-1. The final moments were frantic, with Flamengo surviving late pressure and several more bookings to secure a hard-fought draw in a match that tested their resolve to the limit."
